Tux, the systemLinux mascot
===========================

Tux is the Linux penguin. systemLinux uses him as its mascot (fastfetch shows him too).
The image in this folder (tux.svg, also website/tux.svg) is the standard Tux drawing:

  * Original drawing: Larry Ewing <lewing@isc.tamu.edu>, made with The GIMP.
    https://isc.tamu.edu/~lewing/linux/
    "Permission to use and/or modify this image is granted provided you acknowledge me
    lewing@isc.tamu.edu and The GIMP if someone asks."

  * Vector version: Simon Budig (and Anja Gerwinski), http://www.home.unix-ag.org/simon/penguin/
    Redistribution is free but has to include his README/copyright notice, reproduced in full below.

  * Modern SVG clean-up: Garrett LeSage, https://github.com/garrett/Tux
    Released into the public domain (CC0 1.0).

  * File as published on Wikimedia Commons: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tux.svg

Tux is not the systemLinux logo (that is the wheat ear in assets/logo.png) and does not mean the
Linux Foundation or Linus Torvalds endorse systemLinux. "Linux" is a registered trademark of
Linus Torvalds.

